25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems the catalog-style projects have a lasting legacy, whereas those chasing specific mechanisms often leave their questions unanswered.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We have a surplus of applicants for coding and modelling, but we have lost almost all our trained phenotyping technicians to industry.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The animal facility is now well-covered, but the spectroscopy suite was offline for nearly three months due to a lapsed contract.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Computing is now essentially free under the new agreement, but animal day rates have spiked and shipping costs are rising.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Field sites are currently very volatile due to fire and flooding, though the national repository is finally processing deposits quickly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, if the phenotyping staff are gone, we must be cautious about projects requiring that specific expertise.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree, Shizue. We are strong in computation, but weak in the hands-on technical roles.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if animal rates are rising, any project relying on large colonies will be a financial drain.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Victoria. However, the free computing hours make simulation-heavy work very attractive.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, does the spectroscopy failure affect many of our usual project types?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I also found that biological risks, especially breeding colonies, lead to far more overruns than computational ones.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, it is worth noting that while we have coders, our senior modelling analysts are currently seconded abroad.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Midori, spectroscopy is vital for protein work. If the service contract is a mess, those projects are liabilities.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, that is a blow. We have the junior staff, but the leadership in modelling is temporarily absent.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Midori,,It seems we should avoid field-heavy work and high-maintenance animal colonies if we want stability.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
