50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A: Plant Drought Signaling, B: Regeneration in Amphibians, C: Protein Folding Dynamics, and D: Microbiome Atlas. I favor D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate D is the safest for staffing. A requires phenotyping technicians we no longer have.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I cannot support C because of the spectroscopy issues, and B is too risky given the animal facility costs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,D is computationally friendly and avoids the rising costs of animal units and shipping.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Midori,,"D also avoids the field site disasters I saw, as it is a cataloging effort across zones.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, does the Atlas require the modelling analysts who are currently abroad?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Not primarily. It relies more on sequencing and data organization, which our current applicants can handle.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Midori, the fast repository turnaround you found makes the Atlas even more viable.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, the Atlas also aligns with your finding that catalogs provide the most lasting utility.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. It seems the most robust choice across all our concerns.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am quite happy with D. It is a legacy-building project.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for D. It fits our current workforce.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I vote for D. It avoids the instrumentation and cost traps.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,D is the most logical choice. I vote for D.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Midori,,I also vote for D. It is the most resilient option.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
